all right the past five years have given  players time to come up with some really  advanced tactics and complicated  glitches to take out breath of the  wild's foes with style but today we're  dialing it back a little bit and going  with the easiest simplest tricks to take  on these enemies including hinox talus  lionels guardians and more  some glitches will be used but these are  very simple tricks that don't require  any previous knowledge and are easy to  do if you prefer this type of content  let us know in the comments below  to start off if you see high knocks with  anklets either wooden or metallic these  can be used to repeatedly stun them over  and over if you see one with metal  anklets spring preferably a great  thunderblade swing the blade and drop  the weapon mid-swing to give them shock  properties on the ground then magnesis  it and plop it down right next to the  hinox's leg now you can literally do  whatever you want as long as the blade  is in range it's completely stunned  the wooden anklet is not quite as  abusable but can still give you multiple  chances to distract them simply shoot a  fire arrow at its leg then put it out  with a blizzard rod or ice arrow to  recycle its use  another easy trick is permanent active  hitbox and although this does work  against any enemy it's generally more  effective against guardians and high  knocks by mounting a master cycle or  horse then going at sprinting speeds  attacking holding jump mid attack then  canceling by pressing b your weapon will  now constantly do damage as it's  equipped and can be abused in several  different ways like holding attack with  spear near guardians to bulldoze right  through them  or just spam r and zr back and forth  with a strong weapon near a hinox to  deal damage quickly sometimes before  they can even strike back  if you're up against a talus with a weak  spot on its backside you can make this  fight easier with a couple tools use a  simple korok leaf by attacking jumping  and dropping the bomb quickly this can  sneak the round bomb right between their  legs and detonate it behind them  knocking them down for an easy beating  guardians can be tougher for some new  players because of their oppressive  barrage of laser attacks if it ever  becomes too much though simply cast  magnesius into the air drop any material  on the ground and stand still to get a  breather this will make an invisible  barrier in front of you and you can even  do this on multiple sides if you're  surrounded combine this trick with the  whistle over and over to completely  freeze them in their tracks giving you a  window to strike them in their eye with  an arrow for easy damage  lionel's can be cheesed in a couple ways  depending on your equipment and where  you are the most common and obvious way  is to pummel their face with a  multi-shot arrow over and over waiting  until they shake their head and stun  them again but there are some other  methods such as bringing them near  shallow water imprisoning them in three  cryoness blocks then repeatedly mounting  and attacking it which while mounted on  lynels takes no durability to hit the  lynel but the setup can be a little more  finicky the more approachable trick is  to lasso them with the camera by waiting  until they run off then pointing the  camera downward to control their  movements they will continuously aim for  the top of the screen so just simply  guide them around you in a circle and  hit them with any weapon you'd like  while they're doing this  and the other thing to note is that  every enemy has a weak spot that's  easily struck in bullet time while there  are a multitude of advanced tricks to  get into bullet time whenever you want  make it a little bit easier to access by  simply setting up four bundles of wood  ahead of time to create a permanent  updraft once you have a quick and easy  way to access bullet time over and over  stunning them repeatedly becomes easy  peasy  there's your quick tips to take care of  hyrule's tougher foes if you enjoy a  breath of the wild content stick around  because we still cover this game to this  day like our recent coverage of the  evolution of breath of the wild's  advanced combat for anything else gaming  stick right here on gamespot  [Music]  you
 

